{"id":"n-20261023-wqpjs7","category":"travel","display_title":"Israeli Airlines Shift Focus Amid Security Changes","display_title_he":"חברות התעופה הישראליות משנות מסלול בצל שינויי האבטחה","short_summary":"Israeli carriers have suspended or delayed flights to Morocco and Dubai due to security directives, while US transatlantic services are expanding and lowering prices.","english_level":"C1","words":462,"reading_time":3,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Mini-Moke_%286075905799%29.jpg/960px-Mini-Moke_%286075905799%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"Pedro Ribeiro Simões from Lisboa, Portugal · CC BY 2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mini-Moke_(6075905799).jpg"},"sources":[{"name":"Globes English","domain":"en.globes.co.il","url":"https://en.globes.co.il/en/article-1001560592","title":"El Al too suspends Morocco flights; United expands destinations","published_at":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-22T17:30:00.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-23T08:57:34.058Z","quality_score":8,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["The civil aviation sector in Israel continues to navigate an intricate web of security concerns and operational shifts. In recent days, the commercial flight landscape has witnessed a striking dichotomy: while routes to North Africa and the Persian Gulf face severe disruptions and precautionary halts, transatlantic connections to North America are undergoing a robust expansion, driving airfares down through heightened market competition.","The most recent setback affects travel to Morocco, where Israeli carriers have systematically frozen or scaled back their planned operations. El Al announced that its subsidiary, Sun d'Or, would delay the inauguration of its scheduled route to Marrakech. Originally set to take off on November 16, the launch has been postponed until at least December 15. The flagship carrier explained that it remains in continuous dialogue with defense officials and relevant government authorities to obtain necessary security clearances. To mitigate customer frustration, El Al is offering affected passengers comprehensive resolution packages, including full monetary refunds, future credit vouchers, or complimentary rebooking to European destinations within a narrow three-day window.","This decision mirrors actions taken by competitors Arkia and Israir. Arkia halted ticket sales for its Marrakech services following explicit directives from Israeli security agencies, acknowledging that it is currently evaluating contingent solutions such as commercial code-share partnerships or leased aircraft. Similarly, Israir suspended its ambition to expand operations in Morocco following a security incident involving a flydubai flight, which prompted stringent new security mandates. Meanwhile, the diplomatic and security impasse preventing Israeli carriers from resuming flights to Dubai remains unresolved, as local authorities and Israeli security services have yet to establish a mutually agreeable operational solution.","In stark contrast to the North African and Gulf closures, transatlantic travel from Tel Aviv is experiencing a significant operational renaissance. American carrier United Airlines, which resumed its Tel Aviv to New York services in September following suspensions tied to earlier regional military escalations, is aggressively broadening its flight network from Israel. The airline is scheduled to launch four weekly non-stop flights to Chicago alongside three weekly services to Washington, D.C. Furthermore, looking further ahead, United plans to introduce direct flights connecting Tel Aviv to San Francisco in late March 2027.","This expansion coincides with the recent return of Delta Air Lines and the historic entry of Israir into the long-haul New York route for the first time. With five distinct airlines now vying for transatlantic passengers on the New York corridor, market dynamics have shifted considerably in favor of consumers. Travel market data indicates that average airfares for November have adjusted to approximately $1,223, with Israir offering the most competitive average rate, followed closely by United, Arkia, Delta, and El Al. Industry commentators anticipate that provided global fuel costs remain stable, transatlantic ticket prices could slip below the $1,000 threshold early next year, delivering travelers tangible relief."],"facts":[{"fact":"El Al's subsidiary Sun d'Or has postponed the launch of its Marrakech route, originally planned for November 16, until at least December 15.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"El Al is offering affected passengers options including full refunds, credit vouchers, or rebooking to European destinations within a three-day window without extra charges.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Arkia suspended ticket sales for its Marrakech route following Israeli security directives, and Israir put its Morocco expansion on hold after a flydubai flight incident.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The security impasse preventing Israeli carriers from flying to Dubai remains unresolved.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"United Airlines is expanding flights from Tel Aviv to Chicago (four weekly, starting October 26) and Washington, D.C. (three weekly, starting October 28), in addition to daily flights to New York.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"United Airlines plans to launch flights from Tel Aviv to San Francisco on March 30, 2027.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Five carriers now serve the Tel Aviv-New York route: El Al, Delta, United, Arkia, and Israir.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Average airfares on the New York route for November stand at $1,223, with Israir offering the lowest average price at $1,135.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"civil","lemma":"civil","pos":"adjective","he":"אזרחי","name":false},{"text":"aviation","lemma":"aviation","pos":"noun","he":"תעופה",